    "text": "A lamina is made by removing a small disc of diameter&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> from a bigger disc of uniform mass density and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>, as shown in the figure. The moment of inertia of this lamina about axes perpendicular to the plane of the lamina and passing through the points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></msub></math>​ respectively. If the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mfrac></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math>&nbsp;are the smallest integers,&nbsp;then what is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math>?<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0012128_Ques1_1.jpg\" style=\"width: 232px; height: 204px;\" />",
